# Security Rules

## Security Mindset

Always treat security as a first-class requirement.

Never optimize only for speed of implementation.

Every feature must consider:

- Authentication
- Authorization
- Data privacy
- Tenant isolation
- Input validation
- Error handling


==================================================
OWASP PROTECTION
==================================================

Protect against:

- SQL Injection
- XSS
- CSRF
- Broken Authentication
- Broken Authorization
- Mass Assignment
- Security Misconfiguration
- Sensitive Data Exposure
- Injection attacks


==================================================
AUTHENTICATION
==================================================

Use:

- Devise
- Devise JWT
- JWT


Requirements:

- Access tokens
- Refresh tokens
- Token rotation
- Token expiration
- Logout everywhere
- Session management


Never:

- Store sensitive tokens insecurely
- Expose secrets
- Log credentials


==================================================
AUTHORIZATION
==================================================

Use:

Pundit


Every resource must verify ownership.


Example:

Teacher can only modify assigned classes.

Parent can only view linked children.

Student can only view own data.

Admin can only access own school.


==================================================
MULTI TENANCY SECURITY
==================================================

Tenant isolation is mandatory.


Never trust:

- school_id from frontend
- user supplied tenant identifiers


Tenant context must come from:

authenticated user


==================================================
API SECURITY
==================================================

Implement:

- Rate limiting
- Secure headers
- CORS configuration
- CSP
- HTTPS
- Request validation


==================================================
DATABASE SECURITY
==================================================

Use:

- Foreign keys
- Constraints
- Least privilege database users


Never:

- Expose database IDs unnecessarily
- Return sensitive fields


==================================================
SECRETS
==================================================

Never commit:

- API keys
- Passwords
- Tokens
- Credentials


Use:

- Environment variables
- Secret managers


==================================================
AUDITING
==================================================

Track sensitive actions:

- Login
- Permission changes
- Grade changes
- Attendance changes
- User deletion